WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.256
youtube-to-docs turns videos into
documents to search, share and hear.

00:00:05.606 --> 00:00:08.405
Here's how it works, in six steps.

00:00:09.305 --> 00:00:14.224
Start with a video link, a video
ID, a playlist or a whole channel.

00:00:14.574 --> 00:00:19.029
Playlists and channels are expanded,
and each video runs in turn.

00:00:19.929 --> 00:00:22.143
Next, it gets the words.

00:00:22.493 --> 00:00:25.933
By default, it uses
YouTube's own captions.

00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:31.858
Or it transcribes the audio again
with Gemini, Google Cloud or AWS.

00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:35.683
That gives real word
timings and speaker labels.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:39.846
Either way, you get a
transcript and a timed SRT file.

00:00:40.746 --> 00:00:44.269
Then a language model of your
choice reads the transcript.

00:00:44.619 --> 00:00:50.256
It can run on Gemini, Vertex AI,
AWS Bedrock or Azure Foundry.

00:00:50.606 --> 00:00:53.181
It names the speakers and their titles.

00:00:53.531 --> 00:00:57.727
It pairs each question with its
answer and a timestamp link.

00:00:58.077 --> 00:01:01.318
It writes a summary, a one-sentence
summary and topic tags.

00:01:01.668 --> 00:01:06.411
Gemini can also watch the video,
to read slides and name plates.

00:01:07.311 --> 00:01:09.969
From the summary, it
can draw an infographic.

00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:14.137
Another model looks at the
image and writes its alt text.

00:01:14.487 --> 00:01:18.460
It can read the summary aloud,
and combine both into a video.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.923
And it can make everything
again in a second language.

00:01:22.823 --> 00:01:26.583
Add the -cc flag to make the
original video accessible.

00:01:26.933 --> 00:01:30.088
Captions are corrected,
and each speaker is named.

00:01:30.438 --> 00:01:35.665
They meet WCAG 2.1 Level
AA and Section 508.

00:01:36.015 --> 00:01:39.814
Slides and on-screen text are
described for blind viewers.

00:01:40.714 --> 00:01:43.895
Every output is a file that
you can review and edit.

00:01:44.245 --> 00:01:47.313
Run it again, and the
later steps use your edits.

00:01:47.663 --> 00:01:51.564
A CSV lists every file
and what each step cost.

00:01:51.914 --> 00:01:56.646
Save it all to your computer, Google
Drive, SharePoint or Hugging Face.

00:01:57.546 --> 00:02:02.672
Run it from the command line, the web
app, or as a plugin for your AI assistant.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:07.284
One command takes you from a
link to a full set of documents.

